  "note": "Defence along an anti-tank ditch as IBB Annex V App 9 p 485 draws it: three Coys up behind the ditch (wholly on the home side, not astride it as on a canal), each one Pl up and two back, 450 m apart (500x), the Bn 2750-4115 m (3000-4500x, x = yards); the annex prints a Coy of 1200 m, which with the two gaps passes its own 4115 m: read as about 1200 yd and laid at 1070 m (calc: (4115 - 2 x 450) / 3); depth 1850-2757 m (2000-3000x); mask posns beyond the ditch (App 9: MASK POSN; the 900-1500 m, 100-500x, laid 1200 m beyond the Coys), D Coy and the second line force in depth, counter penetration posns AA and BB on the flanks, dotted; minefields on the far side and in the gaps. The ditch is the ground's, never drawn: click the point on the ditch in front of the centre, aim across it; the Coys' front edge 170 m behind the click (E). Bn HQ (IBB S3 pp 22-24; p 23: placed centrally within the Bn locality, preferably behind the depth localities; a defended locality of 55 all ranks, concealed from the air, dug in, near the Bde axis with an alternative posn; laid beside D Coy, centrally in depth (the distance a decision, E). The RRs, a section of two in each rifle Coy, sited first in the forward localities with an alternative each 200-300 m back (IBB S8 pp 38-42; IC p 367).",
